# Local development values for `wrangler dev` only.
#
# Copy to `.dev.vars` (git-ignored) and fill in. Nothing here is committed and
# nothing here is a production secret: `wrangler dev` reads this file, the
# deployed Worker reads real values from `wrangler secret put`.
#
#   copy .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The OAuth *web client id*. Public by nature (the browser needs it), but kept
# out of git so each deployment's configuration lives in one place.
# Get it from: Google Cloud Console -> APIs & Services -> Credentials ->
# OAuth 2.0 Client IDs -> your "Web application" client.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID="REPLACE_WITH_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID.apps.googleusercontent.com"

# Local dev is plain http, and browsers refuse to store a `Secure` cookie over
# http. Set this to "false" *only* in this file; production stays "true" via
# wrangler.toml.
COOKIE_SECURE="false"

# Origins allowed to call the Worker. Same syntax as wrangler.toml.
ALLOWED_ORIGINS="http://127.0.0.1:*,http://localhost:*"

# Optional. Leave unset to let the Worker choose (Lax for same-host, None for
# GitHub Pages -> *.workers.dev). Uncomment to pin:
# COOKIE_SAMESITE="Lax"
